  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "An object is projected with horizontal velocity $8\\text{ m s}^{-1}$ and upward vertical velocity $5\\text{ m s}^{-1}$. Find the range when it returns to its launch height. Use $g=10\\text{ m s}^{-2}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$8\\text{ m}$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}x(t)&=8t\\\\y(t)&=-5t^2+5t\\end{aligned}$$\n\nAt the launch height, $y(t)=0$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}-5t^2+5t&=0\\\\5t(-t+1)&=0\\\\t&=0\\text{ or }1\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe time of flight is $1\\text{ s}$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{Range}&=x(1)\\\\&=8\\text{ m}\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 31
  },
